language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ candies: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Alice is a kindergarten teacher and wants to give candies to the children in her class. The children sit in a line, each with a rating score. Every child must get at least 1 candy. If two children sit next to each other, the one with the higher rating must get more candies than the other. Alice wants to minimise the total number of candies.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `candies.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/candies.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `candies_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py candies.json
$   savilerow model.eprime candies_1.param -run-solver

$ number of children, derived from the data: the length of ratings (not a field of the reader's JSON)
given ratings_dim1 : int(1..)
$ ratings[i]: rating score of child i, indices 1-based
given ratings : matrix indexed by [int(1..ratings_dim1)] of int

$ x[i]: number of candies given to child i, each at least 1; the upper bound is the number of children, which an optimal allocation never exceeds
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..ratings_dim1)] of int(1..ratings_dim1)
$ z: the total number of candies given out
find z : int(0..ratings_dim1 * ratings_dim1)

minimising z
such that
$ the total number of candies is the sum of the candies given to each child
z = (sum i : int(1..ratings_dim1) . x[i]),
$ between two neighbours, the child with the higher rating gets more candies than the other
forAll i : int(1..ratings_dim1 - 1) . (ratings[i] > ratings[i+1]) -> (x[i] > x[i+1]),
forAll i : int(1..ratings_dim1 - 1) . (ratings[i] < ratings[i+1]) -> (x[i] < x[i+1])
